   "text": "This is selenocystine, two selenocysteine units joined through a Se\u2013Se bond.\n\n- **Chain:** each half is HOOC\u2013CH(NH2)\u2013CH2\u2013Se, and the two CH2\u2013Se units are linked Se\u2013Se. That gives two carboxylic acids, two primary amines, two CH2 groups and two selenium atoms.\n- **Stereochemistry:** both \u03b1-carbons carry a hashed NH2, so both are stereocentres. For the left one, the priorities are N > CH2Se > COOH > H. Viewed with H toward the viewer, N (down), then CH2 (upper right), then COOH (upper left), runs counterclockwise on screen, so the true sense is clockwise. That makes the centre R, the L-configuration for selenocysteine. The right-hand centre is the same by symmetry.\n- **SMILES:** the first centre is written as N[C@@H](C[Se]...)C(=O)O. In the second centre the neighbour order is CH2, H, N, COOH, which swaps N and CH2. The same configuration is therefore written [C@H].\n\nSMILES: N[C@@H](C[Se][Se]C[C@H](N)C(=O)O)C(=O)O"
  }
